author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Accept every supported settings path as an alias in SDK-backed config get/set without bypassing validation; Unknown keys offer at most three nearest legal keys and a working config-list inspection command; Preserve complete legal keys in structured recovery and reject unknown keys without settings writes
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "The SDK accepts supported dotted settings paths through canonical validators, exposes scalar context leaves, returns bounded scope-aware key suggestions and complete SDK legal domains, and routes consent globally."
expected_result: "Settings paths and canonical aliases share validation, persistence and scope; invalid keys or values provide useful recovery without writes."
actual_result: "Linked 67-test config/parser cohort passed after review changes; 199-test combined cohort, source/package/example typechecks and packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx consumers passed. Refusal tests preserve settings/history bytes. Required exact-head CI and bot re-review remain delivery gates on PR #1696."
